{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["This one will comfort us — and if you ask: since they say that Ever was a great prophet who named his son Peleg, why do they not say that Lemech was a great prophet who named his son Noah?! And I, Rashbam, resolved: this one was the first born after the death of Adam, and therefore he named him Noah, saying: May it be His will that this one set right the deterioration of that one. And 'ינחמנו' is the language of prayer — ' comfort us,' may he bring us relief, that is: that he make for us relief and contentment. But in the name 'Noah' the language of prayer does not apply, but rather the language of prophecy. Alternatively, one may say: this was before Noah was born."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "The printed text has 'ותירץ רבנו' (and our Rabbi resolved); I read it as Rashbam's own first-person resolution, which the context demands, and render accordingly."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:44:18.188380489Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}